# Binary assets. Marked so git does not attempt line-ending conversion or
# textual diffs on them.
#
# Not tracked in Git LFS. As of the first committed image (the nowcast progress
# report figures, ~120 KB at REPORT_DPI) the repo holds no other binaries and
# packs to ~19 MB, so LFS would add a required tool for every contributor and
# every CI job to save a fraction of a percent. Revisit if these figures start
# churning per-commit rather than per-milestone: an LFS migration is easy going
# forward, it is only the already-committed blobs that stay in history.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.parquet binary
